  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable tailor-made fertiliser production for improved farming in Madagascar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because of the lack of support by local authorities and the deteriorated business climate in Madagascar.The applicant of this project is The Mauritius Chemical and Fertilizer Industry Limited situated in Port Louis in the Republic of Mauritius. The company started its fertiliser operations in 1975 as a manufacturer of complex NPK granular fertilisers. The local company is Agrival, a Malagasy company that was created in July 2010. Agrival is active in the animal feed industry. After three years, the company has become the country&apos;s major producer and distributor of animal feeds.The partners will establish a joint venture company.While the market for standard fertilisers (such as NPK 11-22-16, DAP and Urea) is efficiently supplied, there is a considerable gap in the market for specific blends. The present demand exceeds 6,500 tons per year. By producing blends Madagascar (which is not the case yet), the project partners aim to cut costs and the project will make agriculture more profitable by enabling even poorer farmers to fertilise their fields. Even more innovative is the fact that the NPK blends will be packed in 1, 3, 5, 10 and 25 kg bags. The project partners will pack in smaller volumes for small-farmers.The blending factory with a total capacity of 20,000 tons of NPK blends per year will be located in Toamasina the most important harbour of Madagascar.</narrative>
  </description>
